#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""maestro-sync: sync a Maestro instance with the template, as a command.

The mechanics of /maestro:maestro-sync (its phases 0 to 6c) with backup
sets under private/backups/. The skill on top of it does the talking; this
command never asks anything.

    plan [--instance DIR] [--plugin-root DIR] [--json]
                    checks the instance root, reads the mirror and working
                    tree paths from private/preferences.md, reports the
                    working tree's state, refreshes the read-only mirror to
                    origin/main, checks the installed plugin against it,
                    then scans the instance and the mirror and writes the
                    plan to private/maestro-sync.plan.json: the changelog
                    slice from the instance's version floor to upstream and
                    one item per thing to do, of kind update (a marked file
                    that differs, the instance's tools: carried over), new
                    (a marked upstream file the instance lacks), bin (the
                    drifted bin/ scripts), retired (a retired path still
                    marked, or the listen unit with its state), register
                    (writing register keys the preferences lack) or orphan
                    (marked here, gone upstream: reported, never removed).
    apply --items ID[,ID...] | --kind KIND [--from FILE] [--register KEY=VALUE ...]
          [--instance DIR]
                    applies items of the last plan, after a backup set at
                    private/backups/<stamp>-sync/ named by the plan's stamp
                    and shared by every apply on that plan: manifest.json
                    first, with every selected item pending, the memory db
                    copied once per set through sqlite3's online backup and
                    checked, every replaced or removed file copied to
                    files/<path> before it is touched, the manifest rewritten
                    after each item. `update` writes the mirror text with the
                    instance's tools: line carried over (or the text of --from
                    FILE as given, for one item: the owner's merge); `new`
                    copies the upstream file; `bin` copies the drifted scripts
                    (mode kept) then runs bin/mem stats with MEM_DB and
                    MEM_SCOPE unset, so a schema migration runs while the db
                    copy is minutes old; `retired` removes a retired path, or
                    the marked members of the listen unit, after re-checking
                    the allowlist and, for listen, that no capture runs
                    (otherwise the item is postponed, nothing is touched, and
                    the run goes on); `register` runs maestro-register-keys
                    write with the --register answers (dotted keys as `plan`
                    lists them; tone_default.synthesis is never set) and moves
                    its backup into the set. --kind update leaves out the
                    items the owner modified locally (stderr: `skipped
                    (locally modified): <path>`); they go through --items.
                    Every applied item appends a line to
                    private/maestro-sync.log. Orphans are never applied. At
                    the end of a run the sets are pruned: the five newest
                    stay, a set younger than seven days stays, at most twenty
                    stay.
    note [ID] --outcome skipped|aborted|kept [--count N] [--instance DIR]
                    appends to the log an outcome the skill decided: an item
                    `(skipped by owner)`, `ABORTED by owner after N files`
                    (no item needed), a retired path or the register keys
                    `(kept by owner)`.
    rollback        not implemented yet
    backups         not implemented yet

`plan` writes only the mirror (clone on first run, fetch, reset) and the
plan file: the instance's other files are read. Without --plugin-root the
repository URL comes from this command's own plugin root and the check
that the loaded plugin is the installed one is skipped, with a warning.
The plan is printed as a readable summary, or as the plan file's JSON
with --json.

`apply` holds private/maestro-sync.lock while it runs (E_LOCKED when
another apply holds it) and refuses a stale plan (E_STALE) when the mirror's
HEAD moved or a file no longer matches the checksum the plan recorded (for
a new file: when its path now exists). A failed item stops the run: the
items before it stay applied, the ones after it stay pending in the
manifest, and the exit code is E_PARTIAL. A postponed listen unit doesn't
stop the run; the exit code is POSTPONED when everything else applied.

Exit codes, always explicit, never a silent degradation:
     0  OK              done
     2  E_USAGE         usage error, or a verb not implemented yet
     3  E_NOT_INSTANCE  not an instance root, or the template repository
     4  E_MIRROR        the mirror, the working tree or a git call failed
     5  E_PLUGIN        the installed plugin can't be checked or is behind
     6  E_STALE         the plan is older than the mirror or than a file
     7  E_ITEM          unknown item, or a bad plan
     8  E_PARTIAL       a write failed after others succeeded
     9  E_LOCKED        another apply holds private/maestro-sync.lock
    10  POSTPONED       the listen unit, while a capture runs
"""

from __future__ import annotations

